<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17224" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτροπ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>not to be turned,
				unchangeable, eternal,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕπνος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Theoc.
					3.49
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>inflexible, rigid,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἅιδης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.483
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρετή</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				10.74
			</span></i> (Paul. Sil.): pr. n., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἄτροπος, ἡ,</span> name of one of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μοῖραι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				905
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				960c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Chrysipp.Stoic.
				2.264
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. Κλωθώ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					3.1337
				</span></i>
			: hence of the decrees of fate, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτροπα γραψάμεναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Epigr.Gr.</u>
					153.4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄ. νόμος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				288
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Cypr.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>uncourteous, unseemly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπεα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
					7.103
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>not turned by the plough, untilled,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Del.</u>
			</span></i>II.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
